React Practical Interview Questions (Basic)

Create a Counter App

Build a counter with Increment, Decrement, and Reset buttons.

Ensure the counter doesn’t go below 0.

Form Handling

Create a simple form with name, email, and password.

Handle state updates, validation (e.g., email must have @), and show errors below input.

Conditional Rendering

Display "Welcome, User!" if a user is logged in, otherwise "Please log in".

Implement a button that toggles login/logout state.

List Rendering

Given an array of objects (e.g., users with id and name), render them as a list.

Add a delete button to remove a user from the list.

Fetching Data with useEffect

Fetch users from https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users and display their names.

Show a loading spinner while fetching, and error message on failure.

Pass Data via Props

Create a Child component that accepts title as a prop and displays it.

Render multiple child components from a parent.

Controlled vs Uncontrolled Components

Show how to make an input a controlled component (using useState).

Convert it into an uncontrolled component (using useRef).

Lifting State Up

Build two inputs: Celsius and Fahrenheit.

When you type in Celsius, Fahrenheit updates automatically, and vice versa.

useEffect Cleanup

Create a component with a timer (setInterval).

Clean it up when the component unmounts.

Basic Todo App

Add a new task.

Mark it as completed.

Delete a task.